      {
        "met_days": 229,
        "type": "flyby",
        "label": "Mars — first successful flyby",
        "description": "Closest approach 9,846 km on 1965-07-15 UTC (1965-07-14 US Eastern) — the first close-up images of Mars ever returned, shattering the pre-spacecraft picture of canals + dense atmosphere. The 22 grainy images revealed cratered terrain resembling the Moon and a thin (4.1–7 mbar) CO₂ atmosphere — Mars looked dead, not Earth-like, and the discovery reshaped a generation of planetary science."
      }
